course: dictionary
lesson: 11837
title: Bleary
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Mum's bleary eyes blinked at the alarm clock.» The clues are the alarm clock and the early start, so bleary describes eyes that are tired and not yet fully awake.
explain: «Ben rubbed his bleary eyes after crying.» Crying makes eyes watery and sore, so bleary can mean watery as well as tired. A bleary-eyed person is someone whose eyes look sleepy, red or unclear.
explain: Bleary can also mean not clear. «Through the bleary window, we could only see the fog.» The window was not clear, so you could not see through it well. Check the clues around the word to find which meaning fits.
fact: «Bleary» is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as eyes or a morning.
fact: «Bleary» means tired, watery or unable to see clearly, especially after sleep or crying.
fact: «Bleary» can also mean not clear, or blurry, like a photo that is out of focus.
fact: «Bleary-eyed» means having tired or watery eyes, often just after waking up.
fact: The comparative and superlative forms are «blearier» and «bleariest».
exercise: «Mia came down to breakfast with bleary eyes, still half asleep.» What does bleary mean here? | *Tired and not fully awake | Very angry | Bright and sparkly | Full of colour
exercise: «The photo was so bleary that we could not tell who was in it.» Find and copy the word that means not clear. | *bleary | who | photo | could
exercise: «He was bleary-eyed after staying up late to finish his book.» What does bleary-eyed suggest? | He could see perfectly well | He was very happy and full of energy | He had won a race | *He was very tired from lack of sleep
test: «After crying, Sara's eyes looked bleary and red.» Why do her eyes look bleary? | Her eyes were closed for a nap | Crying made them watery and tired-looking | She had just won a prize | *Crying made them watery and sore, so they looked tired and unclear
test: Which sentence uses bleary correctly? | The bleary sun shone brightly on the beach. | The bleary football scored a goal. | Bleary is the name of a town. | *The bleary old man peered at the menu because he had left his glasses at home.
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to bleary, as in «bleary eyes»? | Loud | Hungry | *Blurry | Sparkling
